<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Agent sandboxing · Agentic Bible</title><meta name="description" content="How an execution environment restricts code and tools, and why filesystem, network, resource and application boundaries need separate examination."><meta property="og:title" content="Agent sandboxing · Agentic Bible"><meta property="og:description" content="How an execution environment restricts code and tools, and why filesystem, network, resource and application boundaries need separate examination."><meta property="og:type" content="article"><meta property="og:site_name" content="Agentic Bible"><meta property="og:url" content="https://agenticbible.si/articles/agent-sandboxing/"><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary"><meta name="twitter:title" content="Agent sandboxing · Agentic Bible"><meta name="twitter:description" content="How an execution environment restricts code and tools, and why filesystem, network, resource and application boundaries need separate examination."><meta name="robots" content="index, follow"><meta name="color-scheme" content="light"><link rel="canonical" href="https://agenticbible.si/articles/agent-sandboxing/"><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"TechArticle","headline":"Agent sandboxing","description":"How an execution environment restricts code and tools, and why filesystem, network, resource and application boundaries need separate examination.","articleSection":"Capabilities","inLanguage":"en","url":"https://agenticbible.si/articles/agent-sandboxing/","mainEntityOfPage":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://agenticbible.si/articles/agent-sandboxing/"},"citation":["https://gvisor.dev/docs/","https://gvisor.dev/docs/architecture_guide/security/","https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/claude-code-sandboxing"]}</script><link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_astro/Base.DyzAbnuc.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_astro/_id_.w1YKO1jA.css"></head><body><a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="site-header shell"><a class="wordmark" href="/"><img src="/favicon.svg" width="36" height="36" alt=""><span>Agentic Bible<span class="wordmark-sub">A living reference</span></span></a><nav aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="/" aria-current="page">Library</a><a href="/topics/">Topics</a><a href="/about/">About</a><a href="/history/">History</a></nav><a class="header-search" href="/search/" aria-label="Search the library"><svg width="17" height="17" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="8.5" cy="8.5" r="5.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"></circle><path d="m13 13 4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"></path></svg><span>Search</span><kbd aria-hidden="true">/</kbd></a></header><div class="preview-strip" role="region" aria-label="Edition status"><div class="shell"><span class="status-dot"></span> Preview edition <span class="strip-detail">Sourced working drafts. Editorial review pending.</span></div></div><main id="main" class="shell" tabindex="-1"><div class="article-breadcrumb" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><a href="/" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Library</a><span data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>/</span><a href="/topics/capabilities/" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Capabilities</a></div><div class="reading-layout" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><article class="article" data-pagefind-body data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><header id="overview" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><p class="eyebrow" data-pagefind-meta="topic" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Capabilities / Reference entry 12</p><h1 data-pagefind-meta="title" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Agent sandboxing</h1><p class="article-deck" data-pagefind-meta="description" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>How an execution environment restricts code and tools, and why filesystem, network, resource and application boundaries need separate examination.</p><div class="article-status" data-pagefind-ignore data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><span class="draft-pill" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><span class="status-dot" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2></span> Working draft</span><span data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Human editorial certification pending</span></div><nav class="article-actions" aria-label="Article actions" data-pagefind-ignore data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><a href="#sources" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Sources (3)</a><a href="#revision" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Revision history</a><a href="#share" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Share or cite</a><a href="/contribute/?article=agent-sandboxing" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Contribution options</a></nav></header><aside class="contents" data-pagefind-ignore data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><details data-article-contents data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><summary data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>On this page</summary><nav aria-label="On this page" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><a href="#overview" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Overview</a><a href="#the-boundary-needs-a-threat-model" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>The boundary needs a threat model</a><a href="#files-and-network-are-separate-surfaces" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Files and network are separate surfaces</a><a href="#isolation-is-not-unlimited-compatibility" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Isolation is not unlimited compatibility</a><a href="#permissions-and-content-still-matter" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Permissions and content still matter</a><a href="#sources" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Sources & context</a><a href="#revision" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Revision record</a></nav></details><div class="contents-bottom" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><span class="eyebrow" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Part of the collection</span><a href="/topics/capabilities/" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Capabilities <svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2></path></svg></a></div></aside><div class="prose" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><p><strong>Agent sandboxing</strong> restricts the environment in which an agent’s requested code or tools execute. The boundary is implemented by surrounding software and operating-system mechanisms, rather than by asking the model to behave cautiously. gVisor illustrates one design: an application kernel called the Sentry handles application system calls, while a separate Gofer mediates filesystem access. This is a particular isolation architecture, not the definition of every sandbox. <a href="#source-gvisor-overview">1</a></p>
<h2 id="the-boundary-needs-a-threat-model">The boundary needs a threat model</h2>
<p>The gVisor security model aims to reduce exposure to host system interfaces through layered restrictions. It also describes limits: hardware side channels, host resource controls and other reachable services require separate consideration. Its documentation explicitly treats a sandbox as one part of a secure architecture. These statements concern gVisor’s design and assumptions; they do not prove that any environment labeled “sandboxed” provides equivalent isolation. <a href="#source-gvisor-security">2</a></p>
<p>For an illustrative research assistant, the threat model could include a tool accidentally overwriting an unrelated file, untrusted downloaded code running a subprocess, or a generated command attempting an unauthorized connection. A proposed sandbox would need to state which of those actions it constrains and what remains reachable. Listing the threats would be more informative than simply displaying a sandbox badge.</p>
<h2 id="files-and-network-are-separate-surfaces">Files and network are separate surfaces</h2>
<p>Anthropic’s 2025 engineering announcement describes filesystem and network isolation for its agent coding tools. It explains directory restrictions and an external proxy enforcing allowed network destinations, including restrictions applying to subprocesses. This is vendor architecture guidance for the described implementation. It should not be generalized into a claim about current defaults, all coding agents, or a measured security guarantee for this website. <a href="#source-claude-sandbox">3</a></p>
<p>In the research-assistant example, a writable scratch directory would not answer whether the process can also contact arbitrary servers. Conversely, blocking external connections would not answer whether it can modify an unrelated local project. A useful boundary description would separately identify permitted reads, writes and destinations, along with how exceptions are handled.</p>
<p>The relevant unit is the actual executing process and its descendants. Naming the assistant’s top-level tool is insufficient if the command starts other programs with different access. The cited vendor example discusses subprocess coverage; <a href="#source-claude-sandbox">3</a> a different implementation would need its own evidence of what inherits the restrictions.</p>
<h2 id="isolation-is-not-unlimited-compatibility">Isolation is not unlimited compatibility</h2>
<p>gVisor’s overview notes that its Linux-compatible environment does not implement every system call or interface, so some applications may be incompatible. Restricting exposed behavior has practical consequences for what software can run. <a href="#source-gvisor-overview">1</a> A failure inside a sandbox could therefore reflect an intentional boundary or a compatibility gap, rather than evidence that a task needs unrestricted access.</p>
<p>For the example, a denied write would be recorded as denied. A recovery step could choose another permitted way to produce a reviewable artifact, or stop with the boundary stated. It would not silently interpret a failed operation as successful. This is a proposed recovery criterion, not a claim about a deployed assistant here.</p>
<h2 id="permissions-and-content-still-matter">Permissions and content still matter</h2>
<p>The gVisor security model allows applications to use resources exposed inside their environment and relies on additional controls for resource exhaustion and network policy. <a href="#source-gvisor-security">2</a> Isolation consequently does not settle whether a reachable application operation is appropriate. <a href="/articles/tool-permissions/">Tool permissions</a> address that action-level boundary; <a href="/articles/prompt-injection/">prompt injection</a> addresses attempts to redirect the agent through untrusted material.</p>
<p>A sandboxed assistant could still produce an unsupported statement in a permitted output file. Factual review needs different evidence. An <a href="/articles/agent-observability/">observability</a> record could show that a command was denied or completed, while <a href="/articles/human-oversight/">human oversight</a> could decide how to respond. Tests of the example would inspect the actual filesystem, connection policy and action outcome, including subprocess behavior and interruption. Sandboxing can limit consequences within a stated model; it does not certify the whole agent.</p>
</div><p class="article-feedback" data-pagefind-ignore data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><a href="/contribute/?article=agent-sandboxing" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Suggest a correction or primary source</a> · Public intake remains on hold; the local synthetic form covers only the original three entries.</p><section class="sources" id="sources" aria-labelledby="sources-title" data-pagefind-ignore data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><p class="eyebrow" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Follow the evidence</p><h2 id="sources-title" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Sources & context</h2><p data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Primary sources checked on <time datetime="2026-10-17" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>17 October 2026</time>. A source check is not independent editorial approval.</p><ol data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><li id="source-gvisor-overview" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><a href="https://gvisor.dev/docs/" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>What is gVisor? <span aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2></path></svg></span></a><span class="source-publisher" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>gVisor authors</span><p data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Living project documentation checked 17 October 2026; Sentry and Gofer describe an application-kernel isolation design and compatibility boundaries.</p></li><li id="source-gvisor-security" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><a href="https://gvisor.dev/docs/architecture_guide/security/" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>gVisor security model <span aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2></path></svg></span></a><span class="source-publisher" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>gVisor authors</span><p data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Living security design documentation checked 17 October 2026; goals, host interactions, resource controls and hardware-side-channel limitations. No blanket sandbox or virtual-machine ranking follows.</p></li><li id="source-claude-sandbox" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><a href="https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/claude-code-sandboxing" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Beyond permission prompts: making Claude Code more secure and autonomous <span aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2></path></svg></span></a><span class="source-publisher" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Anthropic</span><p data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Engineering announcement published 20 October 2025, checked 17 October 2026; filesystem/network isolation in that product’s described runtime. Vendor-reported statistics and present product defaults are not reproduced here.</p></li></ol></section><section class="revision" id="revision" data-pagefind-ignore data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><h2 data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Revision record</h2><dl data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><div data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><dt data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Authorship</dt><dd data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>AI-assisted project draft</dd></div><div data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><dt data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Source check</dt><dd data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><time datetime="2026-10-17" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>17 October 2026</time>. This records source consultation, not editorial certification.</dd></div><div data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><dt data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Human editorial review</dt><dd data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Pending. No human editorial certification is recorded.</dd></div><div data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><dt data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Latest source change</dt><dd data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><time datetime="2026-10-17" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>17 October 2026</time> · Add six sourced entries on agent operating principles · <code data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>54b9d079</code></dd></div><div data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><dt data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Revision receipt</dt><dd data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>No separate publication receipt is recorded for this working draft.</dd></div></dl><p class="review-scope" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>The twenty entries received deep reading across external and internal review. Claim verification was sampled; this does not certify every factual claim.</p><a class="text-link" data-source-commit="8a38252384c6fe6024a75b462ad95294a131100c" href="https://github.com/Leshey-Digital/agentic-bible/commits/8a38252384c6fe6024a75b462ad95294a131100c/src/content/articles/agent-sandboxing.md" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>View file history on GitHub <svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2></path></svg></a></section><section class="share-tools" id="share" aria-labelledby="share-title" data-pagefind-ignore data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><p class="eyebrow" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Keep a useful reference</p><h2 id="share-title" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Share or cite this entry</h2><p id="article-citation" tabindex="0" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>“Agent sandboxing.” Agentic Bible. https://agenticbible.si/articles/agent-sandboxing/</p><div class="share-buttons" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><button type="button" data-copy-link hidden data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Copy article link</button><button type="button" data-copy-citation hidden data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Copy citation</button></div><p class="share-status" data-share-status role="status" aria-live="polite" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>The citation and link above remain available to 